---
const scenarios = [
  {
    label: 'The leg press is down',
    quote: '“Leg press is out at my gym this week.”',
    body: 'Their AI swaps it for a comparable movement from your programming, same target, same intent, and they’re back to training in the time it takes to read the reply.',
  },
  {
    label: 'No gym for two weeks',
    quote: '“Travelling for two weeks, nowhere to train.”',
    body: 'Their AI rebuilds the block around whatever they’ve actually got, hotel room, bodyweight, resistance bands, so two weeks on the road don’t undo the two months before it.',
  },
  {
    label: 'The rower’s taken',
    quote: '“Rower’s taken and I can’t wait around.”',
    body: 'Their AI has a substitute ready before they’ve finished reading the message. No message to you, no standing around the gym floor.',
  },
];

const chips = [
  'Their own app, not a browser tab',
  'Offline workout logging',
];
---

<section id="client-experience" class="py-21 px-6 bg-ink">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <p class="font-label text-azure text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.24em] mb-3">The client experience</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-text mb-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.875rem,3vw+1rem,2.75rem)] leading-[0.98]">
      Routine questions can be handled without waiting for a live Coach reply.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-text-soft text-lg max-w-2xl mb-11 text-balance">
      Client messages can be handled by an AI configured from your coaching methodology and communication style, within the context Wolvec makes available to it.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-9">
      {scenarios.map((s) => (
        <div class="border border-hairline-dark rounded-2xl p-6 bg-surface-1">
          <h3 class="font-display text-text text-lg mb-2">{s.label}</h3>
          <p class="text-text-soft text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed italic mb-3">{s.quote}</p>
          <p class="text-text-soft text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed">{s.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="text-text-soft text-base max-w-2xl mb-7 text-balance">
      None of it goes around you. Every reply stays inside the autonomy you&rsquo;ve set. Certain reports of pain, injury, illness, dizziness, chest or breathing symptoms, or other physical distress can trigger Wolvec&rsquo;s limited safety controls and be flagged for you. These controls may not identify every concern.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm text-text-soft">
      {chips.map((c) => (
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-azure"></span> {c}
        </span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
